To do a zen Priest I startscummed for fountain-wish on starting room.
After 160 starts I finally got my first blindfold and flawlessly (in
that I only had the blindfold removed to perform the invocation)
ascended.
I decided to go for neutral for more peaceful monsters and chance at
magicbane gift (which I didn't get). With careful play, and some
gauntlets of power I found on DLvl1, the very early game was not so
though as expected, and after exploring first 2 DLevels I camped on DL
1 where there was a co-aligned altar. At around 2700 turns I got
telepathy and at around turn 4300 I got Mjollnir. At this point the
game became very easy. In fact, due to priests ability to ascertain
BUC, after getting telepathy and artifact I think zen priests are
comparable to zen samurais. The second gift I would later receive was
Werebane, which I did not use much.

Sokoban was BoH version, but I already had found one in the upper mine
levels. At Dlvl 10 I found o11c's bones, which had a cloak of magic
resistance. Not much later, while diluting potions on fountains I got
a water demon wish, and wished for SDSM.

The rest of the game was mostly uneventful, apart from the planes;
first, I spend a lot of time on water plane, to the point where I even
wished for a ring of slow digestion: I still had around 50 K-rations,
but I had wishes to burn and I could stay there forever. I kept
noticing where some monsters where disappearing and headed for those
areas, and eventually I found the altar.
Then, on the astral plane, I had a lot of fighting to do, even zapping
a lot of wands of teleport. If I did not have over 500 HP due to
alchemy it would have been though. Also, the riders kept reviving and
and attacking me, sometimes 3 at a time (the right altar was the third
one). On the heat of the fight, I kept zapping my wands of death, and
ended up killing some peaceful priest, committing murder and losing
telepathy. I had brought a tin of floating eye with me, but I kept
being attacked and could not open the tin. Lessons learned: be more
careful with /oD on astral and bring a tin opener. I could have
wished for a [oTelepathy or !MD, but at the time I didn't remember.
Anyway, guided by my stethoscope and warning intrinsic I kept fighting
and teleporting obstacles and eventually I reached the correct altar.

Next I think I will try healer. I think it should be the hardest, so
if I can do it I will probably do the remaining roles. If I can't,
well, I'll stop wasting time on zens :p

